Angular testing tools:
- Jasmine framework for writing and organizing unit testst in a clean and readable f0rmat
- karma framework to run tests and receive test reports
- .spec.ts files.

How Angular Unit tests work:
- writing test suits(collection of test cases)
- defining specs(individual test case withihn suits)
- making assertions(ckecking if a particular condn is met)   

- "ng test" -> starts karma test runner and runs all unit tests in the project

"describe(componentname,function)" -> contains tests for that component
inside function we use "it()" to write the tests

describe('AppComponent',() => {
  it('should have a defined title', () => {
    //assertion
    const component = new AppComponent();
    expect(component.title).toBeDefined();
  });
});

TestBed:
- main api we use to write unit tests

  //for each unit beforeEach() will be executed first
  beforeEach(() => {
    TestBed.configureTestingModule({});
    service = TestBed.inject(UserService);
  })

Fixtures:
- wrapper for the component which has additional functionalities that we can use
let fixture: ComponentFixture<UserListComponent>;
check user-List.Component.spec.ts